+# Two accounts of the Frankel drawing set and the missing 2000-series sheets
+
+Public derivative of the November 10, 2026 source review UTC · STL02–STL03 / AUD011 / AUD016 / B188 / H005. A 2012 article by the FOIA requester and a public 2018 letter describe different accounts of NIST's Frankel holdings. Both identify a gap in the released shop drawings. Their difference matters for locating the piece-specific fabrication sheets used to test candidate identifications for W14A. The actual holdings inventories, cited communication and missing drawings remain unacquired. [2012 release account](https://www1.ae911truth.org/en/ptv-faqs/611-wtc-7-blueprints-exposed-via-foia-request.html) · [2018 letter, p. 2, item 3](https://www.ae911truth.org/images/PDFs/Gage_Letter_to_Copan_102918.pdf#page=2)
+
+| Source | Preserved observation |
+| --- | --- |
+| **NIST response to 12-009**, date stamp **November 23, 2011**, single-page scan, disposition paragraph | NIST records **2,587 electronic files** on **four disks** and says it is releasing those files **“in their entirety.”** This describes the released files. The scan does not give a master drawing index, a per-disk manifest or a count of all holdings. [Verified scan provenance](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/9eae3c08856e37947937a0471de17314cf3e1169/investigation/broader-evidence/steel-frankel-release-scope-2026-11-06/SOURCE-PINS.json) |
+| **Brookman's February 21, 2012 article**, archived publisher page, paragraph beginning with the location of the girder | It says sheets numbered **2001 to 2999** were excluded from the drawings released and reports that the NIST FOIA Office **“indicated they did not have a complete set of the Frankel Steel drawings.”** This is the requester's account of the office's statement. The native statement and its date, meaning and scope remain unverified. [2012 article](https://www1.ae911truth.org/en/ptv-faqs/611-wtc-7-blueprints-exposed-via-foia-request.html#:~:text=all%20sheets%20numbered%20from%202001) |
+| **October 29, 2018 letter to NIST**, physical p. 2 lines 10–14, item 3 | The request calls the missing material the **2000 series** and reports that **“Michael Newman has indicated that NIST had a complete set of fabrication shop drawings.”** The letter records the request and its author's account. The underlying communication, response and any later production remain unverified. [2018 letter](https://www.ae911truth.org/images/PDFs/Gage_Letter_to_Copan_102918.pdf#page=2) |
+| **NCSTAR 1-9 vol. 1**, printed p. 22, §2.4.3 | NIST reports using details from **approximately 2,500 fabrication shop drawings** in structural model development. This is an approximate statement of use. The 2,587 released files include several drawing types. The figures describe separate populations and do not provide an item-level crosswalk. [NIST report](https://tsapps.nist.gov/publication/get_pdf.cfm?pub_id=861611#:~:text=approximately%202%2C500%20fabrication%20shop%20drawings) |
+
+## What the mirror can test
+
+The 2012 account breaks its released total into **22 PDF erection sheets**, **42 TIFF erection sheets**, and **2,523 TIFF fabrication sheets**. The prior Internet Archive mirror's central directory was reparsed directly from the held **524,288-byte** ZIP suffix. It contains **22 PDFs**, **2,565 TIFFs**, one PNG and nine directory entries. The PDF/TIFF total is **2,587**, and **42 + 2,523 = 2,565**. These are container and reported category counts. The match gives no file-for-file evidence of the original four disks or of the TIFF classifications.
+
+The mirror has **2,502** numeric TIFF basenames, including **2000.TIF** and **3001.TIF**, with zero in **2001–3000 inclusive**. Keep the article's **2001–2999**, the 2018 letter's **2000 series** and the mirror's **2001–3000** under their respective sources. The five exact TIFF stems **A2001, A2540, A2568, A2682 and A2696** also returned zero. The basename screen does not inspect drawings under other names. Both capped checks of the publisher ZIP route returned curl **7** and HTTP code **000**, with no response body. That leaves the original publication archive unverified. [Mirror](https://archive.org/download/911datasets/NIST_WTC7_FOIA_12-009.zip) · [Source hashes and access observations](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## What would distinguish the accounts
+
+- [ ] Seek a dated Frankel transmittal, NIST intake list and drawing register, the original statement attributed to the FOIA office and the separate communication attributed to Newman. Test whether they describe the same supplier set, holding date, revisions and notion of completeness. A difference in date or scope is an untested explanation.
+- [ ] Seek original 12-009 disk inventories, any response or enclosures for the 2018 request, and the actual **A2682 / W14×211** fabrication sheet. Join the sheet's mark, stock and detail to the E118 schedule before testing the comparison with W14A's measurements. The 2018 request concerns girder drawings and supplies no explicit W14A join. [Column 14A schedule and specimen limits](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/6bfc9b77a431e83c339dcb79a33ce10125ba4944/investigation/broader-evidence/steel-frankel-column14a-tier-register-2026-11-09/README.md)
+- [ ] Obtain the field measurement and marking records, custody, and the NIST building-attribution worksheet. FEMA's WTC 7 field attribution and NIST's unidentified inventory classification remain separate. A drawing gap does not establish the specimen's building of origin. [FEMA field table, p. 16](https://www.fema.gov/pdf/library/fema403_apd.pdf#page=16) · [NIST inventory, Table A-7](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-C13-799fd8322fd23d7bd4af8d96ea7e58b7/pdf/GOVPUB-C13-799fd8322fd23d7bd4af8d96ea7e58b7.pdf#page=96)
+
+The two newly acquired entities were hashed, selected HTML paragraphs were checked and the letter's relevant item was visually read. The held NIST response scan was rehashed and its disposition paragraph checked. The mirror test covers its complete central directory and selected filenames, with no extraction of additional shop sheets. Earlier source versions and their differing readings remain preserved.
